SUMMARY:🌳 Better Together: The Township Tree Speaks
DESCRIPTION:Center for Spiritual Living Asheville\n# 🌳 Better Together:
  The Township Tree Speaks\n\n## Stories Older Than Asheville Itself\n\nHav
 e you ever wondered what stories a 360-year-old tree could tell?\nJoin **B
 etter Together** for a special outdoor gathering beneath the majestic **To
 wnship Tree**—Buncombe County's oldest known White Oak\, estimated to ha
 ve taken root around **1665**.\n\n📖 **Local historian Jenny Bowen** ret
 urns to share the remarkable story behind this extraordinary tree\, expand
 ing on the history first presented during April's *Rooted in Time* dedicat
 ion ceremony.\n\nTogether we'll explore:\n🌿 Cherokee traditions and loc
 al legend\n🛤️ The disputed Rutherford Trace campaign\n🌎 Centuries 
 of change across this land\n🌳 The Township Tree's recent recognition th
 rough **Asheville GreenWorks' Treasured Tree Program**\n\nThis remarkable 
 oak has quietly witnessed generations of history—long before Asheville e
 xisted. Its story is truly many stories\, making it the perfect gathering 
 place for a community committed to discovering the rich\, layered history 
 we all share.\n\n### 📍 Event Details\n\n📍 **Community Commons at Cen
 ter for Spiritual Living Asheville** *(under the Township Tree — indoors
  if weather requires)*\n🕧 **12:30 PM**\n📅 **Saturday\, August 9**\n\
 n🪑 Bring a lawn chair or blanket\, settle beneath the canopy\, ask ques
 tions\, share conversation\, and deepen your connection to the land and th
 e people who have called it home.\n\n✨ Come listen. Come learn. Come con
 nect.\n\n#CommunityCommonsAsheville #BetterTogether #TownshipTree #Treasur
 edTree #AshevilleHistory #BuncombeCountyHistory #LocalHistory #WhiteOak #C
 ommunityConnection #HistoryMatters #DiscoverAsheville #cslasheville
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/center-for-spiritual-living-asheville
 /events/315940467/
